@startuml
!include _style.iuml
' Adapted from reviewed presentation sources: W2-delivery-ledgers, W3-07a; separate SQL commit / relay / consumer
skinparam dpi 110
skinparam defaultFontSize 18
skinparam ArrowFontSize 17
skinparam ClassAttributeFontSize 17
skinparam ClassStereotypeFontSize 15
skinparam NoteFontSize 16
skinparam LegendFontSize 15
skinparam titleFontSize 20
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam maxMessageSize 165
skinparam nodesep 18
skinparam ranksep 24
hide footbox
hide circle
title DP-2 · candidate with an unprotected dual write
class "Media acceptance" as A <<candidate control>> {
 + adoptSource()
 + publishAfterCommit()
}
class "AcceptedAsset" as B <<candidate entity>> {
 + identity: Identifier
}
class "Broker" as Q <<candidate boundary>> {
 + publishCommand()
}
class "Processing consumer" as C <<candidate control>> {
 + createJob()
}
A --> B : first write: SQL commit
A --> Q : second write: network send
Q --> C
note bottom of C
No durable record connects the two writes.
Candidate roles are explanatory,
not implemented classes.
end note
@enduml
